477
00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.960
Five, shows a lack of motivation.
第五，表现出缺乏动力。

478
00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.640
Kevin responds, hey.
凯文回答说，嘿。

479
00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:43.400
Yeah.
是啊。

480
00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:44.800
Okay.
好吧。

481
00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:45.800
There.
就是这样。

482
00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:46.920
Okay.
好吧。

483
00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.840
There is a blooper that I had never seen.
有一个我以前从未见过的失误镜头。

484
00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.360
I've watched a lot of these bloopers now, right?
我现在看了很多这样的失误镜头，对吧？

485
00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:51.680
Yeah.
是的。

486
00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:55.140
And there's sort of different compilations of them on YouTube.
YouTube上各种合集都有。

487
00:20:55.920 --> 00:21:01.200
I don't know how I missed it, but there is a blooper where Kevin is talking to you at front reception.
我不知道自己怎么漏掉了，有一个失误镜头是凯文在前台接待处跟你说话。

488
00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:01.640
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

489
00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:03.840
And he goes, he said I was dull.
然后他说，他说我很迟钝。

490
00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:05.700
And you can't get through it.
而你根本演不下去。

491
00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:06.820
You keep laughing.
你一直在笑。

492
00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:09.580
I could not do Kevin's scenes.
我根本没法拍凯文的戏。

493
00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:14.380
Brian made me laugh so hard all the time.
布莱恩总是把我笑得前仰后合。

494
00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.060
You had no lines.
你一句台词都没有。

495
00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:16.440
No.
没有。

496
00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.680
All he said was, he said I was dull.
他唯一说的就是，他说我很迟钝。

497
00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:20.860
And you couldn't even look at him.
而且你连看都不敢看他一眼。

498
00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:21.780
I remember that.
我记得那个。

499
00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.160
I remember shooting that.
我记得拍那场戏的时候。

500
00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:23.640
Yeah.
是啊。

501
00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:25.360
Because I don't think we got it.
因为我觉得我们没拍好。

502
00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:28.400
I think the reason it's not in the episode is we never got a take of it.
我觉得这集里没有这个片段是因为我们从没拍出一条能用的。

503
00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:29.260
I couldn't do it.
我做不到。

504
00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.700
I mean, I don't doubt it.
我是说，我并不怀疑。

505
00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:32.060
That happens sometimes.
这种事有时会发生。

506
00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:33.360
Sometimes they were like, you know what?
有时候他们会觉得，你知道吗？

507
00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:34.000
It's a wash.
这就当扯平了。

508
00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:34.540
Never mind.
算了。

509
00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:35.220
Leave it alone.
别管它了。

510
00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:35.940
We have enough.
我们有足够的素材了。

511
00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:36.480
We have enough.
我们有足够的素材了。

512
00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:40.720
And then Dwight in a talking head right after says, I like the people I work with, with the
紧接着德怀特在单人访谈里说，我喜欢我的同事，除了

513
00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:41.820
exception of four.
四个人。

514
00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:42.940
Four people.
四个人。

515
00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:44.280
Who are those four people?
那四个人是谁？

516
00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.060
We got a lot of mail about that.
我们收到了很多关于这事的邮件。

517
00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:46.580
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

518
00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:47.860
Well, what'd you find?
那么，你发现了什么？

519
00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:49.740
I don't know.
我不知道。

520
00:21:50.020 --> 00:21:56.320
People wanted us to name the four people that we think are the four people, with the exception
大家想让我们说出我们认为的那四个人，除了

521
00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:57.020
of four people.
那四个人之外。

522
00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:57.780
Who do you think?
你觉得是谁？

523
00:21:57.780 --> 00:22:00.280
Who do I think he does like or doesn't like?
你觉得他喜欢还是不喜欢？

524
00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.400
No, he says he likes everyone, with the exception of four people.
不，他说他喜欢所有人，除了四个人。

525
00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:05.940
Who do I think he doesn't like?
你觉得他讨厌谁？

526
00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.540
I think he doesn't like Jim.
我觉得他讨厌吉姆。

527
00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:11.080
Oh, Jim is number one on the list for me.
哦，对我来说吉姆排在名单第一位。

528
00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:15.380
I think he doesn't like Creed?
我觉得他讨厌克里德？

529
00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:22.340
I would say Tobey just because Michael hates Tobey and Dwight loves Michael.
我会说是托比，就因为迈克尔讨厌托比，而德怀特效忠迈克尔。

530
00:22:22.580 --> 00:22:23.120
He might.
他可能会。

531
00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:24.520
Well, he likes Pam.
嗯，他喜欢帕姆。

532
00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:25.440
We know that.
我们知道这一点。

533
00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:25.740
Yeah.
对。

534
00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:27.340
He's got a soft spot for Pam.
他对帕姆挺偏心的。

535
00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:29.060
I think he thinks Pam's decent.
我觉得他认为帕姆人还不错。

536
00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:30.720
Maybe Ryan and Kelly.
也许还有瑞安和凯莉。

537
00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:34.020
Maybe Ryan the temp because he's competition.
也许实习生瑞安是因为他是竞争对手。

538
00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:34.500
Yeah.
对。

539
00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.000
To him.
对他的威胁。

540
00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:40.460
And then maybe because he's competitive, maybe one of the other sales reps.
然后也许因为他好胜，也许是其他销售代表中的一个。

541
00:22:40.640 --> 00:22:41.040
I don't know.
我不知道。

542
00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:41.520
Yeah.
是啊。

543
00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:42.960
All right.
好了。

544
00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:43.780
There you go.
就是这样。

545
00:22:43.820 --> 00:22:44.220
We don't know, though.
不过我们也不知道。

546
00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:44.580
We don't know.
我们不知道。

547
00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:45.940
We don't know who the four people are.
我们不知道那四个人是谁。

548
00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:47.180
They were never written down.
剧本里从来没写过。

549
00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:51.360
That's one of those fun little things that we just give you to think about.
那是我们留给你们去琢磨的有趣小细节之一。

550
00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:51.860
Yeah.
对。

551
00:22:51.980 --> 00:22:52.420
The writers.
编剧们。

552
00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:53.540
You tell us who you think.
你们猜猜看是谁。

553
00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:53.880
Yeah.
对。

554
00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:58.880
So now we're in the kitchen, and Jim does an impression of Stanley.
所以现在我们在厨房里，吉姆模仿了斯坦利。

555
00:22:59.180 --> 00:22:59.660
Yes.
没错。

556
00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:03.320
Followed by a Pam talking head doing an impression of Phyllis.
紧接着是一个帕姆的单采镜头，她在模仿菲莉丝。

557
00:23:03.540 --> 00:23:03.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

558
00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:08.820
Tina Kekalik, Michaela Maroney, and Katie Coles all ask this question.
蒂娜·凯卡利克、米凯拉·马罗尼和凯蒂·科尔斯都问了这个问题。

559
00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:13.640
Did the writers know that John could do impressions of Stanley ahead of time,
编剧们是提前知道约翰会模仿斯坦利，

560
00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:16.500
or did they just write it and hope he could do it?
还是只是写了剧本然后祈祷他能做到？

561
00:23:16.900 --> 00:23:23.040
Guys, John Krasinski's impressions were known and legendary.
伙计们，约翰·卡拉辛斯基的模仿可是出了名的传奇。

562
00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:26.920
Guys, we were like 20 episodes in by now, and we were all hanging out a lot.
伙计们，我们当时已经拍了大概20集了，大家经常一起玩。

563
00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:30.200
And in between scenes, or when we were killing time and goofing off,
在拍戏间隙，或者我们打发时间和开玩笑的时候，

564
00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:32.500
John would do these impressions, and we loved them.
约翰就会来上这么几段模仿，我们都超喜欢。

565
00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:37.920
John could be one of those Saturday Night Live people who does impressions of people.
约翰完全可以去当那种擅长模仿名人的《周六夜现场》卡司。

566
00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:40.740
Like, he is an amazing mimic.
真的，他是个绝佳的模仿天才。

567
00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:41.020
Yes.
没错。

568
00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:41.880
The writers knew.
编剧们知道的。

569
00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:42.820
The writers knew.
编剧们是知道的。

570
00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:44.240
It's on the DVD commentary, too.
DVD评论音轨里也提到了。

571
00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:46.900
They talk about it, about how great he is with impressions.
他们谈到了这个，说他模仿得有多好。

572
00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:48.700
I am horrible at impressions.
我可太不会模仿了。

573
00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:52.480
You made me laugh really hard with your Phyllis impression.
你模仿菲莉丝的时候把我逗得前仰后合。

574
00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:58.140
And then here's something I thought was so clever, is your talking head is by the kitchen door
然后这里有个我觉得特别巧妙的地方，就是你的单采在厨房门旁，

575
00:23:58.140 --> 00:24:02.260
that has a window, and over your shoulder, you can see Phyllis and Jim.
那个门上有个窗户，透过你的肩膀，能看到菲莉丝和吉姆。

576
00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:02.600
Yeah.
对。

577
00:24:02.980 --> 00:24:07.120
Which is, Pam has some interesting talking heads location-wise in this episode.
也就是说，这集里帕姆的单采镜头取景位置挺有意思的。

578
00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:07.840
I agree.
我同意。

579
00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:08.340
Yeah.
对。

580
00:24:08.340 --> 00:24:09.640
That was planned.
那是特意安排的。

581
00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:10.220
Yeah.
对。

582
00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:11.880
They wanted you to see them in the background.
他们想让你在背景里看到他们。

583
00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:12.580
Yeah.
对。

584
00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:13.040
Yeah.
对。

585
00:24:13.280 --> 00:24:14.180
Instead of in the chair.
而不是坐在那把椅子上。

586
00:24:14.440 --> 00:24:14.560
Yeah.
对。

587
00:24:14.560 --> 00:24:15.500
Where I normally sit.
我平时坐的地方。

588
00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:20.740
But if you watch the deleted scenes, you can see John doing impressions of more people.
但如果你看删减片段，你会发现约翰模仿了更多人。

589
00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:23.640
So if you want more, you can have more.
所以如果你还想看，这里还有。

590
00:24:23.780 --> 00:24:24.720
And they're great.
而且他们模仿得太棒了。

591
00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:25.280
They're great.
太棒了。

592
00:24:25.380 --> 00:24:27.960
He does several of their, like, members of the office.
他模仿了好几个办公室里的其他人。

593
00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:31.300
At two minutes, 19 seconds, we're in the conference room.
在两分十九秒的时候，我们在会议室里。

594
00:24:31.460 --> 00:24:32.960
Dwight is interrogating Kelly.
德怀特正在审问凯莉。

595
00:24:33.780 --> 00:24:37.300
I swear it looks like rain is going to break at any moment.
我发誓看起来随时都要下雨了。

596
00:24:37.760 --> 00:24:39.480
Well, they could not get through this scene.
哦，他们这场戏根本拍不下去。

597
00:24:39.660 --> 00:24:42.040
I remember this, like, so vividly.
我记得太清楚了，历历在目。

598
00:24:42.420 --> 00:24:44.800
Mindy was, like, on the floor.
敏迪当时直接笑倒在地了。

599
00:24:45.060 --> 00:24:45.140
Yeah.
对。

600
00:24:45.140 --> 00:24:46.160
She had disintegrated.
她整个人都笑瘫了。

601
00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:52.880
And if you watch the scene, when he goes, your ass is on the line, my ass is on the line,
如果你看这个镜头，当他说，你的饭碗不保了，我的饭碗也不保了，

602
00:24:52.980 --> 00:24:54.700
it barely cuts to Mindy.
镜头几乎都没切到敏迪。

603
00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:55.620
It's so quick.
太快了。

604
00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:57.460
Because she couldn't get through it.
因为她根本演不下去。

605
00:24:57.500 --> 00:25:01.360
That might be the only reaction they have where she isn't just giggling.
那可能是他们拍到的她唯一没有在傻笑的反应镜头了。

606
00:25:01.360 --> 00:25:01.780
Yeah.
对。

607
00:25:03.240 --> 00:25:10.800
I feel like rain is about to lose it right after he says, this is not Kelly Kapoor's story hour.
我觉得雷恩在他说完“这不是凯莉·卡普尔的故事时间”之后，差点就笑场了。

608
00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:11.240
Yeah.
对。

609
00:25:11.700 --> 00:25:14.140
Like, he has to, like, purse his lips a little bit.
你看，他不得不稍微抿了一下嘴唇。

610
00:25:14.260 --> 00:25:14.520
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

611
00:25:14.760 --> 00:25:17.240
I want you to notice something in this scene, by the way.
顺便说一句，我想让你注意这个场景里的一个细节。

612
00:25:17.480 --> 00:25:17.720
What?
什么？

613
00:25:18.640 --> 00:25:19.660
Mindy's hair is up.
敏迪把头发扎起来了。

614
00:25:19.880 --> 00:25:20.120
Yeah.
对。

615
00:25:20.940 --> 00:25:22.480
In kind of a twisty thing.
盘成了一种发髻。

616
00:25:22.560 --> 00:25:23.640
It's a stylish twiSt.
是一个很时髦的盘发。

617
00:25:23.900 --> 00:25:24.000
Yeah.
对。

618
00:25:24.300 --> 00:25:25.620
Do you know why her hair is up?
你知道她为什么把头发扎起来吗？

619
00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:27.940
Is it because she got extensions?
是因为她接长发了吗？

620
00:25:28.300 --> 00:25:29.200
For Casino Night.
为了《赌场之夜》那一集。

621
00:25:29.600 --> 00:25:32.140
And we shot Casino Night before this.
而且我们是在拍这一集之前拍的《赌场之夜》。

622
00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:36.920
She's also wearing, like, a colorful shirt, but then, like, this pink sweater shawl thing.
她还穿着一件挺花哨的衬衫，然后外面套着这件粉色毛衣披肩似的东西。

623
00:25:37.060 --> 00:25:38.640
A very fuzzy shawl.
一件非常毛茸茸的披肩。

624
00:25:38.780 --> 00:25:40.000
Half sweater thing.
半截毛衣似的东西。

625
00:25:40.140 --> 00:25:41.480
Like an Angora sweater thing.
就像安哥拉山羊毛衣似的东西。

626
00:25:41.560 --> 00:25:41.740
Yeah.
对。

627
00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:42.500
Yeah.
对。

628
00:25:42.660 --> 00:25:44.420
But anyway, that's why her hair is up.
不过总之，这就是她把头发扎起来的原因。

629
00:25:44.440 --> 00:25:44.660
Well.
好吧。

630
00:25:44.660 --> 00:25:45.500
Because it's longer.
因为头发变长了。

631
00:25:45.860 --> 00:25:46.340
Continuity.
连戏。

632
00:25:46.820 --> 00:25:47.660
That's real good.
这真的很棒。

633
00:25:48.180 --> 00:25:50.580
So next up, Dwight goes over to Ryan.
接下来，德怀特走向雷恩。

634
00:25:50.840 --> 00:25:52.740
He says, I want to search your car.
他说，我想搜查你的车。

635
00:25:53.060 --> 00:25:54.020
Give me your keys.
把钥匙给我。

636
00:25:54.160 --> 00:25:55.160
I want to search your car.
我要搜查你的车。

637
00:25:56.320 --> 00:25:57.480
And Ryan's like, no.
而雷恩说，不。

638
00:25:57.700 --> 00:25:58.480
He's like, no.
他说，不行。

639
00:25:58.660 --> 00:26:00.040
You can't search my car.
你不能搜查我的车。

640
00:26:00.260 --> 00:26:02.860
And then Dwight's like, you want to do this the easy way or the hard way?
然后德怀特就说，你是想用简单的办法，还是困难的办法？

641
00:26:02.960 --> 00:26:03.120
Yeah.
对。

642
00:26:03.580 --> 00:26:04.880
And Ryan's like, okay, what's the hard way?
雷恩就说，好吧，什么是困难的办法？

643
00:26:05.120 --> 00:26:05.300
Yeah.
对。

644
00:26:05.520 --> 00:26:06.480
He's like, I go down.
他说，我走下去。

645
00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:07.060
I get it.
我懂了。

646
00:26:07.120 --> 00:26:08.480
It's like multiple steps.
这就好比有很多步骤。

647
00:26:09.260 --> 00:26:10.800
And Ryan's like, yeah, I'll do it that way.
然后雷恩说，行，我就选那个办法。

648
00:26:11.060 --> 00:26:12.680
Like, he's so, like, cocky.
你看，他真的是太狂妄了。

649
00:26:12.680 --> 00:26:16.900
But through this whole exchange, in the background is Angela Martin.
但在整个对话过程中，背景里站着安吉拉·马丁。

650
00:26:17.080 --> 00:26:19.800
And she has the smuggest look.
她脸上带着无比自鸣得意的表情。

651
00:26:19.940 --> 00:26:20.960
She is so proud.
她太骄傲了。

